just different frequencies,

00:22:41.140 --> 00:22:42.500
I don't know.
- Maybe so.

00:22:42.500 --> 00:22:43.920
- I never had one but
now you made me feel like

00:22:43.920 --> 00:22:44.860
I should get one of those too.

00:22:44.860 --> 00:22:48.510
I should get one of those and
beep myself in a payphone.

00:22:48.510 --> 00:22:52.690
- Well I mean, and you're
the most reliably reachable

00:22:52.690 --> 00:22:54.660
and then you could have a two-way pager

00:22:54.660 --> 00:22:57.800
when you could page something,
you could page a number back.

00:22:57.800 --> 00:22:59.160
I did not have one of those.

00:22:59.160 --> 00:23:03.770
I was not a second-level
manager at IBM as they call it.

00:23:03.770 --> 00:23:07.410
I was just a first-level.
- A peon.

00:23:07.410 --> 00:23:10.040
- So you never even experienced that.

00:23:10.040 --> 00:23:11.171
You never had a beeper.

00:23:11.171 --> 00:23:13.290
- No, I never had a beeper.
- Ha!

00:23:13.290 --> 00:23:15.330
- I never had a reason to have a beeper.

00:23:15.330 --> 00:23:17.928
- Ha!
- Nobody wanted to beep me.

00:23:17.928 --> 00:23:20.590
- What a loser, I mean what
a just unimportant person

00:23:20.590 --> 00:23:22.230
you must have been.
- Yeah I was.

00:23:22.230 --> 00:23:23.800
I was siloed.

00:23:23.800 --> 00:23:25.358
- I was very important.

00:23:25.358 --> 00:23:27.530
I had to be reached.

00:23:27.530 --> 00:23:28.884
- Do you remember--

00:23:28.884 --> 00:23:31.693
- For nothing.
- Dialing 411.

00:23:33.903 --> 00:23:35.130
- Information.

00:23:35.130 --> 00:23:39.950
- Now 411, people use it as
slang, well at least in the 90s.

00:23:41.730 --> 00:23:45.090
I think they still do,
what's the 411 on that,

00:23:45.090 --> 00:23:47.460
give me the download, give me the info.

00:23:47.460 --> 00:23:49.640
And of course this is based on the fact

00:23:49.640 --> 00:23:50.843
that you could dial 411,

00:23:52.552 --> 00:23:57.552
and you still can dial 411 but
this was a reliable service

00:23:58.730 --> 00:24:01.040
before the internet to--
- Yes.

00:24:01.040 --> 00:24:02.344
Well to get a phone number.
- Usually just to get

00:24:02.344 --> 00:24:04.660
a phone number of a place.

00:24:04.660 --> 00:24:07.640
- Yeah, then you could
call them and get the more,

00:24:07.640 --> 00:24:09.315
whatever, talk to 'em.

00:24:09.315 --> 00:24:11.437
- You could also get
an address of a place.

00:24:11.437 --> 00:24:13.060
- Oh really?

00:24:13.060 --> 00:24:15.910
- Yeah you could get information, I think.

00:24:15.910 --> 00:24:17.310
I never used it.

00:24:17.310 --> 00:24:21.447
Literally never used it and I don't know,

00:24:21.447 --> 00:24:24.690
I don't know why 'cause
it's a real person,

00:24:24.690 --> 00:24:26.860
it's not a machine, it's a real person.

00:24:26.860 --> 00:24:28.400
- It still exists?

00:24:28.400 --> 00:24:31.390
- It still exists and
we're going to call it.

00:24:31.390 --> 00:24:33.281
- Ha, okay, all right.

00:24:33.281 --> 00:24:36.153
So are you gonna ask for a number?

00:24:38.970 --> 00:24:41.990
- Well, let's find out, bro.

00:24:41.990 --> 00:24:42.853
- Whatever that means.

00:24:50.055 --> 00:24:50.888
What?

00:24:50.888 --> 00:24:52.805
Let's do it in English.

00:24:54.975 --> 00:24:57.058
What?
- Des Moines, Iowa.

00:25:02.718 --> 00:25:04.190
Resibolsh.

00:25:04.190 --> 00:25:05.023
- What are you doing?

00:25:05.023 --> 00:25:07.800
- [Automated Voice] That's
county of Poke, right?

00:25:07.800 --> 00:25:08.633
- No.

00:25:14.830 --> 00:25:16.480
I would like to speak to a human.

00:25:17.550 --> 00:25:19.000
- You wanna speak to a human?

00:25:22.133 --> 00:25:23.050
Yes!
- Yeah!

00:25:23.920 --> 00:25:26.063
- We're about to get a 411 operator.

00:25:28.290 --> 00:25:30.623
- Yeah, just real quick, I'm actually,

00:25:30.623 --> 00:25:33.460
I don't need a listing in Des Moines,

00:25:33.460 --> 00:25:36.540
but I just wanted, if
you have a quick second

00:25:36.540 --> 00:25:39.453
to just talk about 411 as a service.

00:25:42.950 --> 00:25:44.038
- What?

00:25:44.038 --> 00:25:44.871
(line trilling)

00:25:44.871 --> 00:25:45.704
- Supervisor.

00:25:48.150 --> 00:25:50.760
I'm sorry, yeah, I said Des Moines, Iowa,

00:25:50.760 --> 00:25:54.770
but really what I meant
was, I'm currently talking

00:25:54.770 --> 00:25:57.760
to a friend about 411 service and the fact

00:25:57.760 --> 00:26:01.383
that it still exists and
we wanted to call and just,

00:26:01.383 --> 00:26:05.213
how popular is this service still?

00:26:08.070 --> 00:26:10.312
Oh wow, so--
- What kinda information

00:26:10.312 --> 00:26:11.750
can you get?
- So how long have you been,

00:26:11.750 --> 00:26:13.350
how long have you been doing it?

00:26:14.840 --> 00:26:18.279
20 years, so how much
smaller is the department

00:26:18.279 --> 00:26:20.023
than it was 20 years ago?

00:26:20.905 --> 00:26:22.072
- Can we get--

00:26:26.988 --> 00:26:29.323
- Wow, okay, and we were just talking,

00:26:29.323 --> 00:26:31.630
we used to call to get phone numbers

00:26:31.630 --> 00:26:33.752
but you can get phone numbers, addresses,

00:26:33.752 --> 00:26:36.463
what all can you still get?

00:26:44.170 --> 00:26:45.397
- Yelp reviews?

00:26:45.397 --> 00:26:47.313
- No, can't do Yelp reviews.

00:26:55.340 --> 00:26:57.563
- What movies have you seen lately?

00:27:04.140 --> 00:27:04.973
- Okay.

00:27:05.940 --> 00:27:08.997
Well how about Bob Jenkins
in Des Moines, Iowa?

00:27:08.997 --> 00:27:11.414
(line beeps)

00:27:12.450 --> 00:27:13.920
- Bob Jenkins.

00:27:13.920 --> 00:27:15.210
If you remember--
- I tried.

00:27:15.210 --> 00:27:16.600
- Bob Jenkins, just call back.

00:27:16.600 --> 00:27:20.040
So basically you can't conduct
a relationship with 411.

00:27:20.040 --> 00:27:22.360
They just can't chat.

00:27:22.360 --> 00:27:24.400
- You screwed that up for me, man.

00:27:24.400 --> 00:27:26.540
I was having, that's why I
was telling you be quiet.

00:27:26.540 --> 00:27:28.160
I was having a great
conversation with that woman.

00:27:28.160 --> 00:27:30.150
She completely opened up, she
was like I've been doing it

00:27:30.150 --> 00:27:32.077
for 20 years, it's a
lot smaller, and like,

00:27:32.077 --> 00:27:35.450
"What movies have you seen
lately?" and then she got pissed,

00:27:35.450 --> 00:27:36.869
man, and she wanted to go.

00:27:36.869 --> 00:27:38.308
- She said you couldn't chat.

00:27:38.308 --> 00:27:40.380
- She could have chatted with me.

00:27:40.380 --> 00:27:43.483
That woman would have talked
to me for 17 to 20 minutes.

00:27:44.340 --> 00:27:45.970
And it would have been amazing.

00:27:45.970 --> 00:27:47.560
We didn't even get her name.

00:27:47.560 --> 00:27:52.214
- 20 years of just giving
people exactly what they need.

00:27:52.214 --> 00:27:55.860
That's probably satisfying and draining.

00:27:55.860 --> 00:27:58.590
- She sounds satisfied.
(both chuckle)

00:27:58.590 --> 00:28:00.360
So I never called it, did you call it?

00:28:00.360 --> 00:28:03.480
- I don't recall ever
calling 411 but I'm sure,

00:28:03.480 --> 00:28:07.260
I mean my mom wanted to see if

00:28:07.260 --> 00:28:09.673
the Golden Corral was
open early or something.

00:28:10.920 --> 00:28:12.410
- I just used the phone book.

00:28:12.410 --> 00:28:15.040
- That's so much work,
you gotta like think about

00:28:15.040 --> 00:28:17.430
where things fall in the alphabet.

00:28:17.430 --> 00:28:20.353
Phone book, that's another
thing we don't use anymore.

00:28:20.353 --> 00:28:25.060
I mean they'll still stack
up a phone book in front

00:28:25.060 --> 00:28:27.812
of my house and I'll put it
directly in the recycle bin.

00:28:27.812 --> 00:28:30.389
I feel guilty about it.
- Yeah yeah yeah.

00:28:30.389 --> 00:28:31.490
- Boy that was thrilling.

00:28:31.490 --> 00:28:33.600
I wrote down--
- That was what?

00:28:33.600 --> 00:28:35.160
- Thrilling.
- Oh.

00:28:35.160 --> 00:28:38.710
I didn't know what you said. (chuckles)

00:28:38.710 --> 00:28:41.360
- What about dialing star 69?

00:28:41.360 --> 00:28:42.610
- Oh, now I've done that.

00:28:42.610 --> 00:28:44.283
- Star 69.

00:28:45.170 --> 00:28:48.230
Now if you beeped star 69,
that means something else.

00:28:48.230 --> 00:28:50.451
- It sounds dirty.
- But if you dial star 69,

00:28:50.451 --> 00:28:54.220
it would give you the last
number that called you.

00:28:54.220 --> 00:28:58.350
- Yeah, it was what killed prank calling.

00:28:58.350 --> 00:29:00.410
- Yes.
- But if you were

00:29:00.410 --> 00:29:03.640
prank calling, you could
dial, what could you dial

00:29:03.640 --> 00:29:05.842
to make your number
unlisted before you dial it?

00:29:05.842 --> 00:29:06.820
Star what?

00:29:06.820 --> 00:29:10.370
- Star 68 or something,
there was like, star 96?

00:29:10.370 --> 00:29:13.630
You could block your
call, before you dialed,

00:29:13.630 --> 00:29:16.360
you could do that in order
to block people's ability

00:29:16.360 --> 00:29:17.670
to see--
- I don't know what it was.

00:29:17.670 --> 00:29:18.833
- On caller ID.

00:29:20.073 --> 00:29:21.628
- Yeah you could dial something.

00:29:21.628 --> 00:29:22.537
We did it all the time.

00:29:22.537 --> 00:29:24.840
It was the counter to star 69.

00:29:24.840 --> 00:29:29.840
- Star 69 was, it was like
if the phone was ringing

00:29:30.310 --> 00:29:32.150
and you couldn't get to it.
- Yeah.

00:29:32.150 --> 00:29:34.590
You were kind of, yeah, you
wanted to know who called you.

00:29:34.590 --> 00:29:36.040
- And you didn't have an answering machine

00:29:36.040 --> 00:29:38.230
or they didn't leave an answer.

00:29:38.230 --> 00:29:40.520
I guess it would just drive people nuts

00:29:40.520 --> 00:29:42.970
so they would pay extra.
- Who was that that called?

00:29:42.970 --> 00:29:44.580
- Who was that that called?

00:29:44.580 --> 00:29:45.720
- What?

00:29:45.720 --> 00:29:48.493
Star 67 was how you blocked your number.

00:29:48.493 --> 00:29:50.763
- Blocked being star 69ed.

00:29:51.963 --> 00:29:55.940
- I would assume that this
still all works on landlines.

00:29:55.940 --> 00:29:58.190
Like I said, I've got
one, I'm gonna test it.

00:29:59.569 --> 00:30:02.633
- I don't remember using
that one that much.

00:30:03.600 --> 00:30:06.320
If I didn't answer the phone,
again, you would just like,

00:30:06.320 --> 00:30:09.150
who was that, I don't know,
they'll call back later.

00:30:09.150 --> 00:30:11.920
- We also weren't adults--
- Right.

00:30:11.920 --> 00:30:14.670
- When this was the way things were.

00:30:14.670 --> 00:30:18.710
I think I did, I probably
did it a couple of times

00:30:18.710 --> 00:30:21.520
thinking that maybe I'd gotten
a phone call from a girl

00:30:21.520 --> 00:30:23.510
or something, you know.

00:30:23.510 --> 00:30:25.310
- I remember--
- But--

00:30:25.310 --> 00:30:29.680
- Another thing on my
list that I did do was

00:30:30.720 --> 00:30:34.403
I would, all the phones in
your house were connected,

00:30:34.403 --> 00:30:38.560
so it wasn't like every person
had their own phone line.

00:30:38.560 --> 00:30:40.380
I mean gosh.
- Party line, man.

00:30:40.380 --> 00:30:41.630
Or at least within the house.

00:30:41.630 --> 00:30:45.340
- Yeah within the house
and so if my step-sister

00:30:45.340 --> 00:30:47.010
at the time was talking to her boyfriend,

00:30:47.010 --> 00:30:51.930
I could pick up my
Garfield phone gingerly.

00:30:51.930 --> 00:30:52.930
- His eyes would open.

00:30:52.930 --> 00:30:56.880
- And then I would just like listen.

00:30:56.880 --> 00:30:58.459
I would cover up--
- Hold on.

00:30:58.459 --> 00:31:00.433
- The top hole.
- You eavesdropped.

00:31:00.433 --> 00:31:02.540
- Just listen to this,
see what I could learn.

00:31:02.540 --> 00:31:03.753
- What did you learn?

00:31:03.753 --> 00:31:07.283
- I don't know, nothing, I
don't know, I know a lot now.

00:31:07.283 --> 00:31:09.500
So probably some of it came from them.

00:31:09.500 --> 00:31:12.240
You know, it's like--

00:31:12.240 --> 00:31:16.350
- You were that little brother,
that little step-brother,

00:31:16.350 --> 00:31:17.970
not even half-brother.
- Yeah.

00:31:17.970 --> 00:31:19.860
- That little step-brother.
- I wasn't addicted to it.

00:31:19.860 --> 00:31:23.280
I didn't do it constantly
but I would do it sometimes.

00:31:23.280 --> 00:31:25.210
- Man, violating of privacy.

00:31:25.210 --> 00:31:28.040
I never listened to my
brother's phone calls.

00:31:28.040 --> 00:31:30.150
I was afraid to do that.

00:31:30.150 --> 00:31:33.390
- But the parents could
listen to them too.

00:31:33.390 --> 00:31:34.450
Just get a little, I mean,

00:31:34.450 --> 00:31:36.330
but you would hear that breathing.

00:31:36.330 --> 00:31:38.490
They'd be like, "Get off the phone, Link!"

00:31:38.490 --> 00:31:39.323
I would get that.

00:31:39.323 --> 00:31:41.050
I'm saying she would hear my breathing.

00:31:41.050 --> 00:31:44.490
- You gotta be better than
to let the breaths be heard.

00:31:44.490 --> 00:31:46.253
- Well a man gotta breathe.

00:31:47.720 --> 00:31:51.693
- You pull away from the
microphone to breathe.

00:31:53.370 --> 00:31:56.720
- So, or you would just be on,

00:31:56.720 --> 00:31:59.015
and my mom still has a
landline and I'll call

00:31:59.015 --> 00:32:01.650
and Lewis will answer, I'm talking to him

00:32:01.650 --> 00:32:03.990
and then he'll talk to me for awhile

00:32:03.990 --> 00:32:06.810
and then all of a sudden
he'll just be like, "Sue!"

00:32:06.810 --> 00:32:09.540
And then Mom will get on
the phone in the bedroom,

00:32:09.540 --> 00:32:10.680
then they're both on the phone.

00:32:10.680 --> 00:32:13.458
That's very--
- It's so easy.

00:32:13.458 --> 00:32:15.687
Two people at a speakerphone is--

00:32:15.687 --> 00:32:19.460
- That's something that
is lost, that was nice.

00:32:19.460 --> 00:32:21.000
- And it cannot be replicated.
- Yeah,

00:32:21.000 --> 00:32:22.864
without the landline.
- Two people--

00:32:22.864 --> 00:32:24.630
- I don't have a landline.
- On a close microphone

00:32:24.630 --> 00:32:27.766
speaking into your ear,
it's like a conference call.

00:32:27.766 --> 00:32:31.330
- Yeah it's like I have conference
calls with family members

00:32:31.330 --> 00:32:32.962
all the time, you know?
- Mm-hmm.

00:32:32.962 --> 00:32:37.034
- Mom and Lewis in different
rooms just talking away.

00:32:37.034 --> 00:32:37.867
- Hmm.

00:32:38.740 --> 00:32:39.920
Well--
- I would talk to my mom

00:32:39.920 --> 00:32:42.347
for a long time and then I realized

00:32:42.347 --> 00:32:45.837
Lewis would all of a
sudden after talking to her

00:32:45.837 --> 00:32:48.208
for like 20 minutes, all of a sudden then

00:32:48.208 --> 00:32:50.217
Lewis will be like, "Well, I'm gonna go.

00:32:50.217 --> 00:32:51.213
"I'm gonna let the two of y'all talk."

00:32:51.213 --> 00:32:53.435
It's like oh, he's been
on here this whole time.

00:32:53.435 --> 00:32:54.346
(Rhett laughs)

00:32:54.346 --> 00:32:57.580
I forgot, I kinda forgot
he was still on here.

00:32:57.580 --> 00:32:58.413
Good, good, good.

00:32:58.413 --> 00:32:59.620
- He could take 20 minutes of it.

00:32:59.620 --> 00:33:01.163
I still do have a landline.

00:33:02.730 --> 00:33:06.253
We got it, well, when you get like the--

00:33:06.253 --> 00:33:08.770
- They try to make you get it.
- You get the service

00:33:08.770 --> 00:33:10.700
and stuff, you can get it,

00:33:10.700 --> 00:33:15.700
and my wife was like, yeah let's get it,

00:33:15.970 --> 00:33:18.230
because, you know, we've got kids.

00:33:18.230 --> 00:33:21.670
If they need to get in touch with us.

00:33:21.670 --> 00:33:24.946
'Cause at the time, when we
bought the current house,

00:33:24.946 --> 00:33:26.850
neither of the kids had a cell phone.

00:33:26.850 --> 00:33:28.313
- Right.

00:33:28.313 --> 00:33:31.012
But if they're there and they
need to call 911 or something.

00:33:31.012 --> 00:33:33.668
- And Shepherd doesn't have
a cell phone and sometimes,

00:33:33.668 --> 00:33:37.010
for short stints, he's on his own.

00:33:37.010 --> 00:33:41.330
Like when we go out on the
prairie to bring back a deer.

00:33:41.330 --> 00:33:42.405
- Okay.

00:33:42.405 --> 00:33:46.189
- He'll spend a few fortnights alone.

00:33:46.189 --> 00:33:50.290
(chuckles) No, but a few
minutes alone sometimes,

00:33:50.290 --> 00:33:52.190
and it's like Shepherd,
if anything happens,

00:33:52.190 --> 00:33:54.160
so I remember, I was
like, I had to show them

00:33:54.160 --> 00:33:58.570
how to use the phone and
apparently it's not as simple

00:33:58.570 --> 00:34:02.520
as I remember, at least,
they did not understand,

00:34:02.520 --> 00:34:04.660
no, you pick it up, it's making a noise.

00:34:04.660 --> 00:34:06.159
That's called a dial tone.

00:34:06.159 --> 00:34:08.016
Then you have to press the buttons,

00:34:08.016 --> 00:34:10.431
like just the fact that
they're pressing buttons

00:34:10.431 --> 00:34:12.939
that are not on a touch screen--

00:34:12.939 --> 00:34:14.300
- It's weird.
- They couldn't press them

00:34:14.300 --> 00:34:17.630
all the way in to know that
they had registered the number

00:34:17.630 --> 00:34:19.600
and it's just like all these
little things are like,

00:34:19.600 --> 00:34:21.469
actually you didn't hit
that, you didn't hit it,

00:34:21.469 --> 00:34:23.270
you know why you didn't hit it?

00:34:23.270 --> 00:34:24.620
'Cause you didn't hear it.

00:34:24.620 --> 00:34:27.210
When you hit the number,
you'll hear a (mimics beep),

00:34:27.210 --> 00:34:29.923
the associated tone with
that particular number.

00:34:29.923 --> 00:34:31.688
- Yeah dial--
- Eventually they got it.

00:34:31.688 --> 00:34:34.150
- You're right, the
dial tones don't exist.

00:34:34.150 --> 00:34:36.350
Give me another one off your list.

00:34:36.350 --> 00:34:39.882
- Remembering phone numbers.

00:34:39.882 --> 00:34:41.990
- (chuckles) Right.

00:34:41.990 --> 00:34:45.780
Yeah, there was a time in
our lives when there was like

00:34:45.780 --> 00:34:49.229
drawers in my brain that were dedicated

00:34:49.229 --> 00:34:52.230
to people's phone numbers.

00:34:52.230 --> 00:34:54.110
- I thought we could have
a fun little exercise.

00:34:54.110 --> 00:34:58.917
Now obviously Kiko we're
going to have to edit these.

00:34:58.917 --> 00:35:03.917
But I want to throw out
someone's phone number

00:35:04.550 --> 00:35:06.760
from the past, now let's start with--

00:35:06.760 --> 00:35:08.110
- Well I think it--
- Let's start with,

00:35:08.110 --> 00:35:13.110
I'm gonna start with your
phone number when you lived

